Test fixtures copied from CIRDLES repositories
==============================================

The files under this folder are copied unmodified, byte for byte, from two
public CIRDLES repositories. tests/fixtures/MANIFEST.toml lists every file
with its source repository, source commit, source path, licence and SHA-256.
They were copied on 2026-11-14; the expression and processed-file oracles were added on 2026-11-26.

1. CIRDLES/Tripoli  https://github.com/CIRDLES/Tripoli
   Commit 00dc94109f572c22bb3f357c0f7b1bb5347f62f5 (00dc941, 2026-10-09)
   Copyright 2022 James Bowring, Noah McLean, Scott Burdick, and CIRDLES.org
   Licensed under the Apache License, Version 2.0; a copy of the licence is
   in LICENSE-APACHE-2.0 next to this file. The Tripoli repository has no
   NOTICE file of its own.
   Copied from:
   - TripoliCore/src/main/resources/org/cirdles/tripoli/dataSourceProcessors/
     dataSources/ogTripoli/isotopxPhoenixTIMS/  -> ionvantage/BoiseState/ and
     ionvantage/KU_IGL/NBS981-500_20191208-5563.xls
   - TripoliCore/src/test/resources/org/cirdles/tripoli/core/reporting/
     dataFiles/IsotopxPhoenixTIMS/              -> timsdp/
     shortReports|cycleReports|fullReports/IsotopxPhoenixTIMS/
                                                -> oracle/<same folders>/
   - TripoliCore/src/test/resources/org/cirdles/tripoli/core/expressions/
     NBS981_210325b-392_ExpressionEval.txt          -> oracle/expressions/

2. CIRDLES/tripoli-manual  https://github.com/CIRDLES/tripoli-manual
   Commit 8b52824b9104e10238322d29898844b3e6ec750e (8b52824)
   Files: testData/GHR1 20200827-11 Pb-6590.xls and
          testData/GHR1 20200827-11 U run2-6591.xls
          -> ionvantage/KU_IGL/
   Licence: the repository has no LICENSE file. The manual's pages declare
   "license: CC-BY-4.0" in their front matter (for example
   setup/03-QuickStart.md, author Noah McLean, University of Kansas). We read
   that as covering the repository's test data too, but the repository does
   not say so explicitly. Attribution: Tripoli User Guide, CIRDLES
   (Noah McLean, James Bowring, Scott Burdick), CC BY 4.0,
   https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/.

Tripoli is CIRDLES's name. This project is not Tripoli and is not endorsed by
CIRDLES; it uses these files only as test inputs and expected outputs.

